# Response templates for the code-task handlers (issue #1177).
#
# Debugging guidance, regex and SQL composition, shell-command composition,
# structural code explanation, review, test generation, refactoring, and
# format conversion render their prose through these records so no response
# text lives in Rust. Placeholders in braces are filled by the handler.

multilingual_responses
  response response_code_debugging_defect_en
    intent code_debugging_defect
    language en
    text "A defect in a function named `{name}`.\n\nWhat the name promises: a function named `{name}` must return {property} ({grounding}).\n\nDetected defect (code line {line_no}): `{line}`\nThe expression applies the binary `{shift}` to the whole quotient: `/` binds tighter than `-` and `+`, so this computes ({fixed}) {shift}, not the value the name promises.\n\nFix — drop the shift so the promised value is returned unchanged:\n    {fixed}\nor, if the shift was meant to apply to an operand of the division, move it inside the divisor so it applies there, not to the quotient:\n    {parenthesized}\n\nMethod, stated honestly: a structural scan — the operator precedence of the token stream was checked against the property the function name promises (the `function_intent` records in data/seed/meanings-code-structure-explanations.lino). No code was executed and no test was run; the canonical form for this property is `{correct_form}`."
  response response_code_debugging_index_bound_en
    intent code_debugging_index_bound
    language en
    text "A loop bound past the end of `{collection}`.\n\nDetected defect (code line {line_no}): `{line}`\nThe bound `{bad}` lets the index reach the length of `{collection}`, one past its last valid position, so the final pass reads `{collection}[…]` out of range.\n\nFix — stop one position earlier:\n    {fixed}\n\nMethod, stated honestly: a structural scan against the index-bound table (`index_bound_past_end` in data/seed/code-task-cues.lino), confirmed by an index into `{collection}` in the same code. No code was executed and no test was run."
  response response_code_debugging_condition_assignment_en
    intent code_debugging_condition_assignment
    language en
    text "An assignment where a comparison was meant.\n\nDetected defect (code line {line_no}): `{line}`\nThe condition assigns with a single `=`, so it tests the assigned value instead of comparing: the branch runs whenever that value is truthy, and the variable is overwritten.\n\nFix — compare instead of assigning (in JavaScript, `===` is the strict comparison):\n    {fixed}\n\nMethod, stated honestly: a structural scan of each condition that opens with a head from the condition table (`assignment_in_condition` in data/seed/code-task-cues.lino) for a lone `=` at the top level of its parentheses, outside quoted text. No code was executed and no test was run."
  response response_code_debugging_no_defect_en
    intent code_debugging_no_defect
    language en
    text "No recognized defect pattern.\n\nThis is a debugging request and the code was scanned, but no construct in the defect table matched: the table currently covers a binary `+`/`-` applied at top level after a division (a shifted quotient), cross-checked against the property the function name promises, a loop bound that lets an index reach a collection's length, and an assignment inside a parenthesized `if`/`while` condition.{intent_note}\n\nMethod, stated honestly: structural scan only — no code was executed, no test was run, and nothing outside the table was guessed. Next steps a human would take: run the failing input, read the traceback, and compare the output against the property the function name promises."
  response response_regex_synthesis_pattern_en
    intent regex_synthesis_pattern
    language en
    text "Composed regular expression:\n\n```regex\n{pattern}\n```\n\nHow the constraints composed:\n{mapping}{anchor_note}\nVerified structurally: groups are balanced, every repetition is well-formed, and every character class is closed.\n{execution}"
  response response_regex_synthesis_not_executed_en
    intent regex_synthesis_not_executed
    language en
    text "Not verified by execution: no example could be derived from these constraints, so no match was run against any input. Test the pattern on real inputs (a regex tester or a unit test) before relying on it."
  response response_regex_synthesis_witness_verified_en
    intent regex_synthesis_witness_verified
    language en
    text "Verified against examples derived from the constraints: the pattern text was matched by the subset matcher in rust/src/solver_handlers/regex_witness.rs (anchors, classes, groups and repetitions read from the pattern itself) and accepted all {positive_count} positive examples ({positives}) and rejected all {negative_count} negative examples ({negatives}). No input of yours was run; test the pattern on your real inputs before relying on it."
  response response_regex_synthesis_witness_failed_en
    intent regex_synthesis_witness_failed
    language en
    text "The check against examples derived from the constraints failed (+ marks an example that should match, - one that should not): {failures}. Do not rely on this pattern; restate the counts and separators and I will compose it again."
  response response_regex_synthesis_broken_en
    intent regex_synthesis_broken
    language en
    text "I will not guess a pattern. The constraints composed to `{broken}`, which failed structural verification ({problems}). Restate the counts — how many of which character class, separated by what — and I will compose it again."
  response response_regex_synthesis_refusal_en
    intent regex_synthesis_refusal
    language en
    text "I could not derive composable constraints from this request, so I will not guess a pattern. I compose from counts of character classes ('five digits', 'two letters'), optional groups ('optionally followed by a hyphen and four digits'), and separators (hyphen, dot, slash, colon, comma, underscore, space). Name the classes and counts explicitly and I will compose the pattern."
  response response_sql_synthesis_statement_en
    intent sql_synthesis_statement
    language en
    text "Composed SQL:\n\n    {statement}\n\nClause-by-clause mapping:\n{mapping}Verified by construction: each clause above maps to one constraint in the request, and the statement is a single SELECT in standard syntax.\nNot verified by execution: this project carries no SQL engine or parser dependency, so nothing was run — check the column names against your actual schema before running it."
  response response_sql_synthesis_refusal_en
    intent sql_synthesis_refusal
    language en
    text "I could not identify a table in this request, so I will not guess one. Name the table ('from the users table', 'select all users') and I will compose the SELECT. Verified by construction only: nothing was run against a database."
  response response_shell_command_composed_en
    intent shell_command_composed
    language en
    text "Composed shell command:\n\n    {command}\n\nFlags, from the {package} manual:\n{flags}Manual: {manual}\n\nDerivation: {derivation}\nNot executed: this is a composed suggestion — run it yourself and inspect the output."
  response response_shell_command_piped_en
    intent shell_command_piped
    language en
    text "Composed shell command:\n\n    {command}\n\nFlags, from the {package} manual:\n{flags}Manual: {manual}\n\nPiped into {pipe_tool}, flags from the {pipe_package} manual:\n{pipe_flags}Manual: {pipe_manual}\n\nDerivation: {derivation}\nNot executed: this is a composed suggestion — run it yourself and inspect the output."
  response response_shell_compose_refusal_en
    intent shell_compose_refusal
    language en
    text "This request reads as a shell task, but no manual-page entry in data/seed/manual-pages.lino covers it (find, ls, head, tail, grep, wc and sed are covered), so I will not guess a command. Say which files, sizes, ages, paths, line counts, or patterns are involved and I will compose it."
  response response_code_explanation_lines_en
    intent code_explanation_lines
    language en
    text "A structural explanation, line by line. No code was executed.\n\n{lines}Coverage: {matched} of {total} lines matched a construct; every line is listed above, each matched one with the reference that defines its construct.\nOverall: {overall}\n{cost}Method, stated honestly: each line was matched against the construct table in data/seed/meanings-code-structure-explanations.lino; nothing was run and nothing outside the table was guessed."
  response response_code_explanation_no_construct_en
    intent code_explanation_no_construct
    language en
    text "No construct in the table matched these lines. The table covers function definitions, for loops, if statements, comprehensions, sum/len/max/min calls, comparisons, assignments, returns, division, indexing, method calls, and a few JavaScript constructs. Method, stated honestly: structural scan only — no code was executed. If the code uses constructs outside the table, a human read (or a language-server hover) will explain more than I can derive structurally."
  response response_code_review_findings_en
    intent code_review_findings
    language en
    text "Structural review against data/seed/code-review-rules.lino. No code was executed; no linter was run.\n\nFindings:\n{findings}"
  response response_code_review_no_match_en
    intent code_review_no_match
    language en
    text "No rule in the review table matched this code. That is a statement about the rule table, not a clean bill of health: the table covers bare except, mutable default arguments, == None, string += in loops, and JavaScript loose ==. Run a real linter (ruff, eslint) for a deeper review. Method, stated honestly: structural scan only — nothing was executed."
  response response_test_generation_suite_en
    intent test_generation_suite
    language en
    text "Generated pytest suite (Python). NOT executed — executing generated tests is out of scope here (that is issue #1185's scope); review the cases and run them yourself with `pytest -q`.\n\n```python\n{suite}```\n\nDerivation: {derivation}"
  response response_code_refactoring_async_en
    intent code_refactoring_async
    language en
    text "Rewrote the promise chain with async/await. Handler bodies are preserved verbatim; only the control flow changed.\n\n```javascript\n{code}```\n\nEquivalence check, stated honestly: structural — each `.then(handler)` became a `const <param> = await <previous>;` in try-block order and `.catch(handler)` became the catch clause, so every handler still receives what the previous link produced. No code was executed."
  response response_code_refactoring_refusal_en
    intent code_refactoring_refusal
    language en
    text "Recognized a refactoring request, but the only structural transformation implemented is a JavaScript promise chain (`.then`/`.catch`) to async/await, and this code has no promise chain, so I will not guess a different rewrite. Name the transformation you want (or show a promise chain) and I will do that one."
  response response_format_conversion_to_yaml_en
    intent format_conversion_to_yaml
    language en
    text "Converted JSON to YAML. Subset, stated honestly: nested objects, arrays, strings, numbers, booleans, null — block style, two-space indent; flow style, anchors, tags and multi-line scalars are outside it.\n\n```yaml\n{yaml}```\nRound-trip check: re-parsing this YAML with the same subset parser reproduced the input JSON exactly, so the conversion is reversible within the subset."
  response response_format_conversion_to_json_en
    intent format_conversion_to_json
    language en
    text "Converted YAML to JSON. Subset, stated honestly: block-style mappings and sequences, two-space indentation, scalars (numbers, booleans, null, plain or quoted strings); flow style, anchors, tags and multi-line scalars are refused rather than guessed.\n\n```json\n{json}```\nRound-trip check: parsing the emitted JSON back reproduced the same values and nesting as the input YAML."
  response response_format_conversion_refusal_en
    intent format_conversion_refusal
    language en
    text "I will not guess a conversion. {reason}"
  response response_mapping_line_en
    intent mapping_line
    language en
    text "  - '{request}' -> {emission}\n"
  response response_flag_line_en
    intent flag_line
    language en
    text "  - `{flag}` — {meaning}\n"
  response response_code_debugging_no_intent_en
    intent code_debugging_no_intent
    language en
    text " Note: the function name `{name}` is not in the intent table, so there was no promised property to check the code against."
  response response_regex_mapping_line_en
    intent regex_mapping_line
    language en
    text "  - '{label}' -> `{render}`{role}{separator}\n"
  response response_regex_role_main_en
    intent regex_role_main
    language en
    text " (the main run)"
  response response_regex_role_optional_en
    intent regex_role_optional
    language en
    text " (an optional group)"
  response response_regex_role_required_en
    intent regex_role_required
    language en
    text " (a required group)"
  response response_regex_note_separator_en
    intent regex_note_separator
    language en
    text " preceded by a literal `{literal}`"
  response response_regex_anchor_note_anchored_en
    intent regex_anchor_note_anchored
    language en
    text "  - anchored with ^ and $ so the whole string must match, not just a substring\n"
  response response_regex_anchor_note_unanchored_en
    intent regex_anchor_note_unanchored
    language en
    text "  - not anchored (the request asked to match a substring), so the pattern matches anywhere\n"
  response response_regex_problem_dangling_escape_en
    intent regex_problem_dangling_escape
    language en
    text "a backslash at the end escapes nothing"
  response response_regex_problem_bad_repetition_en
    intent regex_problem_bad_repetition
    language en
    text "a repetition count is missing after an opening brace"
  response response_regex_problem_unclosed_repetition_en
    intent regex_problem_unclosed_repetition
    language en
    text "a repetition count is not closed"
  response response_regex_problem_unbalanced_parens_en
    intent regex_problem_unbalanced_parens
    language en
    text "unbalanced parentheses"
  response response_regex_problem_unbalanced_class_en
    intent regex_problem_unbalanced_class
    language en
    text "unbalanced character-class brackets"
  response response_code_explanation_line_en
    intent code_explanation_line
    language en
    text "  - `{line}` — {meaning} ({grounding})\n"
  response response_code_explanation_unmatched_line_en
    intent code_explanation_unmatched_line
    language en
    text "  - `{line}` — no construct in the table matches this line, so it is left unexplained rather than guessed\n"
  response response_code_explanation_overall_en
    intent code_explanation_overall
    language en
    text "the function name `{name}` promises {property}; the canonical expression of that promise is `{correct_form}` ({grounding}).\n"
  response response_code_explanation_no_overall_en
    intent code_explanation_no_overall
    language en
    text "the function name is not in the intent table, so there is no promised property to summarize.\n"
  response response_code_explanation_cost_linear_en
    intent code_explanation_cost_linear
    language en
    text "Cost: a single pass over the input, so the work grows linearly (O(n)).\n"
  response response_code_explanation_cost_constant_en
    intent code_explanation_cost_constant
    language en
    text "Cost: no loop over the input appears in these lines.\n"
  response response_code_review_finding_en
    intent code_review_finding
    language en
    text "  - [{severity}] {title} — line {line_no}: `{line}`\n    {advice}\n    {source}\n"
  response response_format_conversion_csv_to_json_en
    intent format_conversion_csv_to_json
    language en
    text "Converted CSV to JSON. Data rows: {rows}; header columns: {columns}. CSV carries no types, so every value stays a JSON string rather than a guessed number or boolean.\n\n```json\n{json}```\nRound-trip check: parsing the emitted JSON back gave every row the same value under every header column as the CSV it came from."
  response response_format_conversion_reason_csv_en
    intent format_conversion_reason_csv
    language en
    text "The text is outside the supported CSV subset (a header row of unique, non-empty names, then at least one row with the same number of comma-separated fields, double-quoted fields with doubled quotes inside), so I will not guess a conversion."
  response response_format_conversion_reason_bad_json_en
    intent format_conversion_reason_bad_json
    language en
    text "The text was recognized as JSON but could not be parsed ({detail}), so I will not guess a conversion."
  response response_format_conversion_reason_roundtrip_en
    intent format_conversion_reason_roundtrip
    language en
    text "The conversion was composed, but re-parsing it did not reproduce the input exactly, so I will not show a possibly-wrong result."
  response response_format_conversion_reason_subset_en
    intent format_conversion_reason_subset
    language en
    text "The text is outside the supported YAML subset (block mappings, block sequences, two-space indent, scalars), so I will not guess a conversion."
  response response_test_generation_unknown_shape_en
    intent test_generation_unknown_shape
    language en
    text "Recognized a request for tests of `{function}`, but its name matches no problem shape in the test-case table ({shapes}) and the request states no example with its expected value, so I will not guess what it must return. State examples as a call followed by its expected value, such as `{function}(<input>) returns <expected>` with a number, a quoted string, a list, True, False or None, and each one becomes a test case."
  response response_test_generation_refusal_en
    intent test_generation_refusal
    language en
    text "Recognized a test-writing request, but no function under test could be identified — name it, ideally in backticks like `is_palindrome(s)` — so I will not guess test cases."
  response response_regex_synthesis_execution_verified_en
    intent regex_synthesis_execution_verified
    language en
    text "Verified by execution in the browser worker: the pattern was compiled with the JavaScript RegExp engine and matched all {positive_count} positive examples derived from the constraints ({positives}) and rejected all {negative_count} negative examples ({negatives})."
  response response_regex_synthesis_execution_failed_en
    intent regex_synthesis_execution_failed
    language en
    text "Execution check failed in the browser worker: {failures}. Do not rely on this pattern; restate the counts and separators and I will compose it again."
  response response_code_refactoring_execution_matched_en
    intent code_refactoring_execution_matched
    language en
    text "Execution check in the browser worker, beyond the structural check: the original chain and the rewrite both ran against recording stubs for every free identifier in {scenarios} scenarios (every call fulfilled, then each of the {calls} calls rejecting in turn), and the recorded call traces matched. Fulfilled trace: {trace}."
  response response_code_refactoring_execution_mismatch_en
    intent code_refactoring_execution_mismatch
    language en
    text "Execution check in the browser worker found a difference between the original chain and the rewrite ({detail}). Review the rewrite before relying on it."
  response response_code_refactoring_execution_skipped_en
    intent code_refactoring_execution_skipped
    language en
    text "Execution check in the browser worker was skipped ({detail}); only the structural check above applies."
